  "description": "<div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><div style='margin-bottom:3rem;'><div><div style='max-width:100%; display:inherit;'><div style='font-family:inherit;'>Cascadia Bioregion boundaries were delineated based on the boundaries of watersheds. The definition of which watersheds to use was based primarily on the Cascadia Institute's publications (cascadia-institute.org/).<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'>Delineation of the bioregion was completed in a Lambert Azimuthal Equal Area coordinate system using data from the North American Environmental Atlas.<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><br /><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'>Data sources:<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'>1) Watershed boundaries - Center for Environmental Cooperation. 2011. Watersheds. www.cec.org/north-american-environmental-atlas/watersheds/<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'>2) Countries and land - Center for Environmental Cooperation. 2010. Political Boundaries. www.cec.org/north-american-environmental-atlas/political-boundaries-2010/.<\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div>",
